WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:09.180
Michael Bloomberg has just pulled 13 and 14%
in two national polls and we've got to talk

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.010
about what is the path.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:17.300
Michael Bloomberg, particularly if the DNC
dissatisfied with Joe Biden's disastrous performance

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.010
in Iowa, decides that maybe they want to change
establishment horses midstream.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:27.490
So remember the DNC changed the rules a few
days ago to at least potentially allow Michael

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:32.200
Bloomberg into upcoming debates despite the
fact that he's not accepting individual donors,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.790
which up until now had been a requirement
to make the debates.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:43.690
He now needs 10% in approved polls and incredibly
13 and 14% in two polls.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:50.350
Bloomberg is in third place, either by himself
or tied with Elizabeth Warren in two polls.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:57.100
Now morning consult from a couple of days
ago has it as Biden 28 Bernie 24 Warren and

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.700
Bloomberg tied at 14 and Pete boot edge edge
back at six.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:10.310
Then in the Harris poll, you have Biden 31
Bernie 20 and Bloomberg 13 one point ahead

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.310
of Elizabeth Warren.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:17.209
Of course, statistically within the margin
of error, this needs to translate to votes,

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.209
right?

00:01:18.209 --> 00:01:19.209
That's the thing.

00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:24.789
So these numbers suggest to me that indeed
the DNC, the DNC is going to have to decide

00:01:24.789 --> 00:01:30.289
in their effort to deny Bernie the candidacy
and enlight of Joe Biden's poor performance

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:31.360
in Iowa.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.840
Do they want to get behind peed, booed, edge
edge?

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.909
Do they want to, it seems less likely, but
maybe get behind Amy Klobuchar the other kind

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:43.939
of establishment centrist or do they want
to start looking at Michael Bloomberg who

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:50.090
of course has effectively an unlimited amount
of money to spend a, has more than $55 billion,

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:55.009
personally has already poured between one
and 200 million into ads and potentially would

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:59.810
do a lot more if the DNC were to get behind
them, behind him.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.689
But then what happens in individual States?

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:07.560
That's also a question because Bloomberg skipped
Iowa and New Hampshire, barely a blip in Nevada,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.360
South Carolina, almost not there.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.099
Bloomberg's focused on super Tuesday.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:17.250
So you know, polling zero in Nevada, but no
polling since January.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.700
Maybe he could end up doing better.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:25.030
They're pulling zero in South Carolina, but
that poll is 10 days old in California and

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:29.469
Texas, he's actually doing something between
four and 7%.

00:02:29.469 --> 00:02:33.730
The national support will mean nothing unless
he can start accumulating delegates.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:37.739
I said before, I think he may do it starting
on super Tuesday.

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:41.219
Uh, but if he doesn't, then this will all
be essentially for nothing.

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:43.590
So where do you think Bloomberg's going?

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:58.890
Will

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:23.459
the DNC

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:40.340
get

00:03:40.340 --> 00:04:42.229
behind him?

